1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
This video introduces the upgraded 3D pen virtual model function and its related function updates.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,000
First, you can draw in the area outside the model.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:16,000
You can directly draw the clothing version in the 3D environment without having to start from the 2D version.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:23,000
You can not only draw the curve on the model surface, but you can also freely draw in the surrounding 3D environment.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:27,000
It makes it easier to build complex three-dimensional outlines.

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Now let's re-create the outline of the chest according to the reference clothing.

7
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,000
You can directly see how to use the function after upgrading.

8
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,000
First, select the 3D pen virtual model tool.

9
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:42,000
When you select it, you will see a line of hints appearing next to the light.

10
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:48,000
You can just click on the model to place it.

11
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,000
Press the P key to create a template outside the model surface.

12
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:56,000
In this example, I will start from the model surface.

13
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:01,000
Then extend outward to create a three-dimensional skirt.

14
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Let's start from using the 3D pen.

15
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Draw a curve along the model's body.

16
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Now let's draw the 3D version.

17
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Here I will press the P key.

18
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:25,000
As shown, this function allows you to copy the model.

19
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Free extension of the line to the 3D environment.

20
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:33,000
At the same time, a guide point will appear to let you directly check the X, Y, and Z axis.

21
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:36,000
Easy to determine the position of each expansion point.

22
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Blue represents the Z axis, red represents the X axis, and green represents the Y axis.

23
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:44,000
Just like drawing on the model, when you are drawing in the 3D area,

24
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:47,000
You can also press the Ctrl key to draw a curve.

25
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:52,000
To improve accuracy, when you are drawing in the 3D environment, you can also press the Shift key.

26
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:55,000
This will be 45 degrees in the 3D window.

27
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:57,000
This will create 8 guide points.

28
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:01,000
Your view and mouse cursor will automatically align these guides.

29
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:04,000
This will allow you to draw more accurately in the 3D environment.

30
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Once you release the Shift key, the guide will disappear.

31
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Next, press the D key to show a curve.

32
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:17,000
And show the actual distance between the mouse pointer and the model.

33
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Press the D key again to close the function.

34
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:23,000
When you have completed the drawing in the 3D area,

35
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Click the point where you first drew and the area where you drew.

36
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:37,000
Click and press the 3D pen to display the tool.

37
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Then select the flat version tool.

38
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:44,000
A tool will appear next to your cursor.

39
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:47,000
It will prompt you to select the area to be generated and press the return key.

40
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Select a section of your version and press the return key.

41
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:59,000
In this way, a flat version will be generated in the 3D window.

42
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:03,000
You can see it in the 2D window at the same time.

43
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:06,000
Using the 3D pen virtual model function after upgrading,

44
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:12,000
You can directly draw in the 3D area outside the model and model.

45
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,000
It allows you to draw faster in the design process

46
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:18,000
and combine multiple dimensions to create the flat version you want.

47
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:21,000
It helps you to create the complex design you imagine more easily.

48
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:28,000
Next, I will introduce to you

49
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:32,000
other advantages of 3D pen virtual model.

50
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:36,000
First, you can use the 3D pen virtual model tool

51
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:42,000
to select the line in the 3D window by pressing the drag and drop button.

52
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:46,000
Of course, you can also use the shortcut ctrl and a to select all the lines.

53
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,000
The next update is that

54
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:51,000
in the menu of the 3D line, press the right button.

55
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:56,000
It will increase the option of display length.

56
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:59,000
After pressing the cancel option in the blank,

57
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:02,000
it will not display and only display in the selected state.

58
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:04,000
If you need to hide it,

59
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:07,000
you only need to use the same operation to hide the measurement length.

60
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:12,000
The next update is that the 3D-painted line can be copied to the edge of the grid.

61
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:17,000
This function allows the 3D pen line to be automatically copied along the virtual model grid path.

62
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:20,000
In order to improve the accuracy and speed of creation or adjustment of the version,

63
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:22,000
when using this option,

64
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:25,000
the line will be aligned with the recent grid edge.

65
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:32,000
Next, I will introduce to you the function of the 3D pen virtual model.

66
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:35,000
Now, in addition to being able to 3D-painted multiple sheets at a time,

67
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:37,000
you can also merge them into one.

68
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,000
First, select multiple closed areas.

69
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,000
Press the return button directly.

70
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:45,000
You can see that there are multiple sheets that have been sewed in the 2D window.

71
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:47,000
Delete the sheet.

72
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,000
Now, when I operate again,

73
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:54,000
you can see that the 3D pen is now 3D.

74
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:56,000
You can see the tool prompt.

75
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:58,000
You need to press the Shift and return keys.

76
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:01,000
At this time, there is only one sheet in the 2D window.

77
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:06,000
This improvement greatly simplified the work of converting the 3D block into a 2D sheet,

78
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:09,000
speeding up the process and reducing manual operation.

